# Built by scripts/demo-corpus.ts — build products, never committed.
#
# `.demo-pack` and `.demo-pack-author` are the pack round trip: the fixture
# needs a pack written by SOMEBODY ELSE, so a throwaway corpus is built, exported
# as a pack, and imported. Both land beside `.demo-corpus` rather than inside it,
# because a pack the corpus contains is a pack the corpus already has — measured,
# that round trip reports `0 new, 0 changed, 4 identical` and the screen draws a
# pack that carried nothing.
.demo-corpus/
.demo-pack/
.demo-pack-author/

# harness scratch
.scratch/

# Playwright MCP session artefacts.
.playwright-mcp/
e2e/screens/

# A CONVERSATION COPY MUST NEVER REACH GIT — owner ruling 2026-09-09, "the
# conversation files should be git ignored so no sensitive data would be saved
# in git".
#
# Every path that holds conversation-derived data today is ALREADY covered and
# was verified rather than assumed: `.my_context/.index.db` above,
# `.my_context/.audit|.revisions|.staging|.statusline|.verdicts|state` by their
# own `*` files, `e2e/screens/` directly above (which matters more than it
# looks — those PNGs render his real transcript, and 0 are tracked), and
# `mycontext conversation persist` writing to `~/.my-context/conversations/`,
# outside the repository entirely. Checked with `git grep`: no tracked file
# carries a credential shape, and no tracked `.jsonl` carries a transcript
# record. The twelve tracked `.jsonl` are `harness/evidence/*` CLI captures.
#
# THIS RULE IS FOR THE ONE HOLE THAT REMAINED. `MYCONTEXT_MIRROR_DIR`
# (`core/conversation-mirror.ts`) overrides the mirror root and can point it
# ANYWHERE, including inside this tree — a test, a script or a slip. A mirror is
# a WHOLE TRANSCRIPT, so that is the one case where a full conversation could
# land in a tracked location, and nothing ignores `*.jsonl` generally (nor
# should it: the harness evidence above is tracked deliberately).
#
# Named by directory rather than by extension for that reason. Verified nothing
# tracked sits under a `conversations/` path before adding it.
conversations/
*.transcript.jsonl

# RETRIEVAL RESULTS AND THE MISSIONS THAT PRODUCED THEM — `plan:recall seq:2`,
# spec §9. Same ruling as the block above and the same reason, applied to a new
# directory rather than restated: a result file is assembled FROM conversation
# text, so it is conversation text, and it is a working artefact rather than
# corpus. It is not `reports/` either, which is hand-written narrative and is
# tracked on purpose.
.my_context/.retrieval/
